{"schema":1,
"kind":"trace",
"id":"fence_area",
"source":"fence_area.py",
"code":"import sys\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    raw = sys.stdin.read()\n    data = raw.split()\n    w = int(data[0])\n    limit = int(data[1])\n\n    hi = (w - 1) // 2\n    hi = min(hi, limit)\n    low = w // 4\n    nxt = low + 1\n    best_x = 0\n    best_area = -1\n    for pick in (low, nxt):\n        x = min(hi, pick)\n        x = max(1, x)\n        area = x * (w - 2 * x)\n        if area > best_area:\n            best_x = x\n            best_area = area\n\n    print(best_x, best_area)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n",
"alt":"The program reads the wire length w and the limit on x, works out the largest allowed x, then tries the whole number w // 4 and the one above it, clamps each into the allowed range, computes the area x * (w - 2 * x) and keeps the larger.",
"presets":[
